        "The boundary is linear in the predictors because the log-odds are linear.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Scaling and Pipelines\n",
        "\n",
        "For unpenalized logistic regression, scaling does not change the fitted probabilities except for numerical details. For penalized logistic regression, scaling is important because the penalty is applied to coefficients.\n",
        "\n",
        "The usual predictive workflow uses a pipeline."
      ],
      "id": "32f15462"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import cross_val_score\n",
        "\n",
        "pipe = Pipeline(\n",
        "    steps=[\n",
        "        (\"scaler\", StandardScaler()),\n",
        "        (\"model\", LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000)),\n",
        "    ]\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "scores = cross_val_score(\n",
        "    pipe,\n",
        "    cancer.data,\n",
        "    cancer.target,\n",
        "    cv=5,\n",
        "    scoring=\"accuracy\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "scores.mean()"
      ],
      "id": "c8cba3f3",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "This fits the scaler inside each training fold, avoiding data leakage.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Penalized Logistic Regression\n",
        "\n",
        "Logistic regression can be regularized just like linear regression. The common penalties are:\n",
        "\n",
        "- ridge penalty: shrinks coefficients toward zero;\n",
        "- lasso penalty: can set some coefficients exactly to zero;\n",
        "- elastic net penalty: combines ridge and lasso.\n",
        "\n",
        "In `sklearn`, the parameter `C` controls regularization strength:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "C=\\frac{1}{\\lambda}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Smaller `C` means stronger regularization."
      ],
      "id": "f988d37a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.model_selection import GridSearchCV\n",
        "\n",
        "pipe = Pipeline(\n",
        "    steps=[\n",
        "        (\"scaler\", StandardScaler()),\n",
        "        (\n",
        "            \"model\",\n",
        "            LogisticRegression(\n",
        "                penalty=\"l1\",\n",
        "                solver=\"liblinear\",\n",
        "                max_iter=1000,\n",
        "            ),\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "    ]\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "param_grid = {\n",
        "    \"model__C\": np.logspace(-3, 2, 20),\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "grid = GridSearchCV(\n",
        "    pipe,\n",
        "    param_grid=param_grid,\n",
        "    cv=5,\n",
        "    scoring=\"accuracy\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "grid.fit(cancer.data, cancer.target)\n",
        "\n",
        "grid.best_params_"
